46
00:02:42,960 --> 00:02:44,860
I haven't decided a cloud provider.

47
00:02:45,030 --> 00:02:48,720
I haven't decided the eventual
production hosting model.

48
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:51,740
I don't even know whether
the architecture I have

49
00:02:51,780 --> 00:02:54,390
today will still be the
architecture I need in

50
00:02:54,430 --> 00:02:57,330
several episodes from
now. So, I want a runtime

51
00:02:57,370 --> 00:03:02,820
that gives Articulate some useful
capabilities now without unnecessarily

52
00:03:02,860 --> 00:03:06,120
constraining where the
platform can evolve.

53
00:03:06,180 --> 00:03:10,230
And with that criteria
established, I can finally look

54
00:03:10,270 --> 00:03:14,420
at the candidates. This is
where I expected decision

55
00:03:14,460 --> 00:03:17,560
to become easier. It didn't.

56
00:03:18,180 --> 00:03:20,840
Because once I started evaluating
the candidates against the

57
00:03:20,880 --> 00:03:24,300
requirements from the previous
episodes, several of them could

58
00:03:24,340 --> 00:03:26,800
