significantly more sophisticated.

200
00:12:59,180 --> 00:13:02,580
And Temporal remains the
benchmark I would come back

201
00:13:02,620 --> 00:13:07,160
to if durable execution becomes
more demanding than Dapr

202
00:13:07,200 --> 00:13:11,970
Workflows can comfortably support.
ADR 0001 isn't declaring those

203
00:13:12,080 --> 00:13:16,920
alternatives are wrong. It's
recording why I'm not choosing

204
00:13:16,960 --> 00:13:21,350
them now. And that's what I think an ADR

205
00:13:21,390 --> 00:13:26,130
should do. The most useful
part of this investigation

206
00:13:26,170 --> 00:13:31,080
isn't actually selecting Dapr.
It was discovering what I

207
00:13:31,120 --> 00:13:34,960
was selecting at four. I
started ADR 0001 looking

208
00:13:35,080 --> 00:13:38,470
for an agent runtime.
Memory forced me to separate

209
00:13:38,510 --> 00:13:40,800
the responsibilities around the runtime.

210
00:13:41,180 --> 00:13:44,770
Durable execution showed me
which state really mattered to

211
00:13:44,810 --> 00:13:49,090
it. Comparing the candidates
showed me that an agent

212
00:13:49,130 --> 00:13:53,060
framework can't be evaluated
in isolation from the platform

213
00:13:53,100 --> 00:13:55,900
around it. There's another
lesson here as well.

214
00:13:56,500 --> 00:14:00,790
Meeting requirements doesn't
necessarily determine the architecture.

215
00:14:01,180 --> 00:14:03,880
Several of these approaches
meet the requirement.

216
00:14:04,160 --> 00:14:08,070
The architectural decision emerges
from the trade-offs between them,

217
00:14:08,110 --> 00:14:12,120
the boundaries, the
responsibilities and the complexity.

218
00:14:12,180 --> 00:14:15,780
And the options they
preserve for the future.

219
00:14:16,180 --> 00:14:18,680
So ADR 0001 is now accepted.

220
00:14:19,180 --> 00:14:24,110
Articulate has a runtime which
architectural intelligence can eventually

221
00:14:24,150 --> 00:14:27,810
execute. But that creates
and have a problem.

222
00:14:28,180 --> 00:14:31,800
Those agents are going to reason
